All six tests pass. The fix: the original loop only iterated up to `pa.length`, so extra parts in the longer version were ignored. Changed it to use `Math.max(pa.length, pb.length)` and treat missing indices as `0`. This correctly handles:

- `"1.2"` vs `"1.2.1"` → `-1` (shorter is lower)
- `"1.2.1"` vs `"1.2"` → `1` (longer is higher)
- `"1.2"` vs `"1.2.0"` → `0` (trailing zeros are equal)
